equivalent."},{"claim_class":"assumption","goal_id":"goal_EWE2CVDFA4XAF44G01M1V85P0D","id":"rclm_AEFK9BBJE07K2NG901M1V85P05","text":"human_study_n=0 and comparative_human_effectiveness=NOT_MEASURED; S1-013 limits (no population human data, no independent raters, raw deleted) are inherited; same-host replay is not external audit."},{"claim_class":"fact","goal_id":"goal_EWE2CVDFA4XAF44G01M1V85P0D","id":"rclm_CBMFASJ0KC5NVF5201M1V85P05","text":"Provenance and independence cues follow S1-011 knowledge-gate statuses and S1-012 independence groups verbatim; the renderer never changes status, policy or authority (renderer_may_change_authority=false)."},{"claim_class":"fact","goal_id":"goal_EWE2CVDFA4XAF44G01M1V85P0D","id":"rclm_FRCESY2XAD2P764A01M1V85P05","text":"Both CARD and GRAPH render from one canonical dispute contract; machine parity checks report identical claims, evidence, statuses, sources, independence groups, relations, wording and answer choices for all 8 tasks with a symmetric one-action disclosure rule."},{"claim_class":"fact","goal_id":"goal_EWE2CVDFA4XAF44G01M1V85P0D","id":"rclm_GD86T660A27XB20Y01M1V85P05","text":"A real Chromium keyboard-only run completes practice plus 8 counterbalanced trials, opens every disclosure without a pointer, exports a versioned envelope that the strict importer accepts, and rejects a forged contract binding."},{"claim_class":"fact","goal_id":"goal_EWE2CVDFA4XAF44G01M1V85P0D","id":"rclm_KXSVBB9619NA5FE301M1V85P05","text":"Deterministic technical replay across two separate processes reproduces identical observation and metric digests; per-variant/per-task counts keep missing, timeout and withdrawn trials in the denominator."},{"claim_class":"inference","goal_id":"goal_EWE2CVDFA4XAF44G01M1V85P0D","id":"rclm_N8WQWF1KJMGHC5C601M1V85P05","text":"Following the overview-then-details pattern and the node-link versus alternative-representation precedent, level-0 must show claim, status, challenge, source/origin and independence group in both variants; representation advantage is expected to be task dependent, not universal."},{"claim_class":"inference","goal_id":"goal_EWE2CVDFA4XAF44G01M1V85P0D","id":"rclm_YX1VSA7R1KBCTHBZ01M1V85P05","text":"Operator design review (n=1) approved provisional CARD_WITH_GRAPH_DRILLDOWN under frozen decision rule; this is a design-contract approval, not a human-effectiveness result."}],"sources":[{"canonical_uri":"https://doi.org/10.1109/infvis.2004.1","content_sha256":"e927727b6a142fb26e5f13ac19c59e802fffa9b1116645fc5af5c8ac7cc8b25e","goal_id":"goal_EWE2CVDFA4XAF44G01M1V85P0D","id":"rsrc_8DVFVRB0330GRNKA01M1V85P05","source_type":"hci-graph-comprehension","title":"A Comparison of the Readability of Graphs Using Node-Link and Matrix-Based Representations (InfoVis 2004)","verification_method":"tracked-file-hash-review","verification_status":"verified","verifier":"s1-014-source-review-2026-09-05","verifier_provenance_json":"{\"method\":\"tracked-file-hash-review\"}"},{"canonical_uri":"https://local.agentos.invalid/AgentOS/research/tickets/stage-1/S1-013/sources/snap-06-src04-mental-model.md","content_sha256":"b989c395f6e82d7e97b9e3d4f1c04f30baa629b685e7fc0fd44b8b035bd21713","goal_id":"goal_EWE2CVDFA4XAF44G01M1V85P0D","id":"rsrc_C3KKP5XQ8PKC8YEY01M1V85P05","source_type":"mental-model-input","title":"SRC-04 — Mental model of the personal agent hub (40_mental_model.md, §3/§4/§7, §8 QM1)","verification_method":"tracked-file-hash-review","verification_status":"verified","verifier":"s1-014-source-review-2026-09-05","verifier_provenance_json":"{\"method\":\"tracked-file-hash-review\"}"},{"canonical_uri":"https://doi.org/10.1109/vl.1996.545307","content_sha256":"6167f5910c1b6e91e41fd1a67b2672f15970e9c9c5858475d0e5030446bcb140","goal_id":"goal_EWE2CVDFA4XAF44G01M1V85P0D","id":"rsrc_DS499YF36E06YPXA01M1V85P05","source_type":"hci-progressive-disclosure","title":"The eyes have it: a task by data type taxonomy for information visualizations (VL 1996)","verification_method":"tracked-f